(7733899, 1274554, 141319, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ErinKirsten:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by roz:</b></div><hr/><i> btw .. it could be a breed thing .. but I could never imagine my Tod posing so chill with something like that on his head .. <br/>having said that it could just be that you are a dog whisperer .. :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>He has been posing for years now, he LOVES it.  This particular time, once I got the photo; I had forgotten to bring his treats in and he wouldnt leave the area until I went and got the treats and gave him some.  As though I couldnt be trusted!  LOL. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>My dogs all LOVE to pose. In fact going into the "studio" (aka my spare bedroom) is a mission, because they all storm in wanting to be "the model for the day" :-)</td>', 'Originally posted by ErinKirsten: Originally posted by roz: btw .. it could be a breed thing .. but I could never imagine my Tod posing so chill with something like that on his head .. having said that it could just be that you are a dog whisperer .. :)   He has been posing for years now, he LOVES it.  This particular time, once I got the photo; I had forgotten to bring his treats in and he wouldnt leave the area until I went and got the treats and gave him some.  As though I couldnt be trusted!  LOL.   My dogs all LOVE to pose. In fact going into the "studio" (aka my spare bedroom) is a mission, because they all storm in wanting to be "the model for the day" :-)', '2022-12-05 01:35:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(7733900, 1274543, 141319, '<td valign="top">I saw too late that my post was shoddy on the BG ... will have to fix that before giving it to the owner.<br/>I photographed the whole litter and this one was really shy initially. We took her off set, photographed the others and then put her and a sibling back in - that did the trick and she really came out of her shell.</td>', 'I saw too late that my post was shoddy on the BG ... will have to fix that before giving it to the owner.I photographed the whole litter and this one was really shy initially. We took her off set, photographed the others and then put her and a sibling back in - that did the trick and she really came out of her shell.', '2022-12-05 01:38:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(7733901, 1274555, 141319, '<td valign="top">Congratulations Roz - its all about the light ... Beautiful<br/> <br/>Pls,pls can you explain how you got the BG? I have some cicada exoskelletons on a tree and wanted to take "exactly" this shot, but don''t seem to get it right ... Of course it would have been great to get the animal emerging the "old" body, but that happened during the night I guess.</td>', 'Congratulations Roz - its all about the light ... Beautiful Pls,pls can you explain how you got the BG? I have some cicada exoskelletons on a tree and wanted to take "exactly" this shot, but don''t seem to get it right ... Of course it would have been great to get the animal emerging the "old" body, but that happened during the night I guess.', '2022-12-05 01:42:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(7733902, 1274573, 141319, '<td valign="top">Oh, I thought this would do much better</td>', 'Oh, I thought this would do much better', '2022-12-05 01:43:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(7733923, 1274555, 67145, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kasaba:</b></div><hr/><i> Congratulations Roz - its all about the light ... Beautiful<br/> <br/>Pls,pls can you explain how you got the BG? I have some cicada exoskelletons on a tree and wanted to take "exactly" this shot, but don''t seem to get it right ... Of course it would have been great to get the animal emerging the "old" body, but that happened during the night I guess. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>hey Gaby .. i''ll answer you here in case anyone is interested .. <br/>for starters here is the original photo .. <br/><a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1274746" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/65000-69999/67145/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1274746.jpg" xalt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/65000-69999/67145/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1274746.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/65000-69999/67145/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1274746.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''"/></a> <br/>i''m not sure what you mean about the background .. but if you mean about the blur then its all about the aperture .. and how close you are to the insect and how close it is to the background .. if that makes sense .. <br/>i feel a bit weird telling you this as you are an amazing photographer ... and probably know what i''m telling you anyway .. <br/> <br/>if you wanted to know about the other stuff .. like the colours etc .. <br/>looking at my working tif file i can see that i did a sunlight action in Nik color efex .. <br/>to get the warmer colours i used an overlay that i can share with you if you want it .. <br/>i used the gradient tool in different colours to get the light top rhs .. and did a brightness and contrast adjustment layer to give it a boost ..  <br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by kasaba: Congratulations Roz - its all about the light ... Beautiful Pls,pls can you explain how you got the BG? I have some cicada exoskelletons on a tree and wanted to take "exactly" this shot, but don''t seem to get it right ... Of course it would have been great to get the animal emerging the "old" body, but that happened during the night I guess.   hey Gaby .. i''ll answer you here in case anyone is interested .. for starters here is the original photo ..  i''m not sure what you mean about the background .. but if you mean about the blur then its all about the aperture .. and how close you are to the insect and how close it is to the background .. if that makes sense .. i feel a bit weird telling you this as you are an amazing photographer ... and probably know what i''m telling you anyway ..  if you wanted to know about the other stuff .. like the colours etc .. looking at my working tif file i can see that i did a sunlight action in Nik color efex .. to get the warmer colours i used an overlay that i can share with you if you want it .. i used the gradient tool in different colours to get the light top rhs .. and did a brightness and contrast adjustment layer to give it a boost ..   ', '2022-12-05 02:10:19.000000', NULL, 0),
